{
  "name": "Pstore: social posting router (6 platforms)",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "SOCIAL POSTING ROUTER — point pstore's SOCIAL_WEBHOOK at the \"Inbound webhook\" URL below (POST /webhook/pstore-social). Pstore fires one webhook per published kit with the exact payload documented in app/social.py:\n\n{\"body\", \"link\", \"platform\", \"name\", \"slug\", \"keyword\", \"board\", \"image\", \"image_png\"}\n\nThis workflow normalises that payload, then routes it to every platform whose toggle is ON in the \"Normalize payload\" node's TOGGLES constant (flip a flag to true once you have that platform's credentials).\n\nWHAT EACH BRANCH POSTS (via plain HTTP Request nodes):\n- X / Twitter   -> POST /2/tweets (OAuth 2.0 user context; X now requires a paid dev app)\n- Facebook      -> POST /photos on a Page (Graph API access token)\n- LinkedIn      -> POST /v2/ugcPosts (Bearer token from a LinkedIn app)\n- Instagram     -> media container -> /media_publish (IG business + FB Graph token)\n- Pinterest     -> POST /v5/pins (OAuth2 token from your approved Pinterest app)\n- Threads       -> /threads -> /threads_publish (Threads app access token)\n\nREALITY CHECK (no tool 'gives' you extra posting accounts): X, Instagram and Threads require YOUR OWN developer app, approved per platform, on EVERY automation tool — n8n, Make or Zapier. Only Facebook, LinkedIn and Pinterest can be authenticated with a plain token. Telegram is covered by the older pstore-fanout-social.json and needs no approval."
      },
      "id": "00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001",
      "name": "Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -900,
        -500
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "httpMethod": "POST",
        "path": "pstore-social",
        "responseMode": "onReceived",
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000002",
      "name": "Inbound webhook",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.webhook",
      "typeVersion": 1.2,
      "position": [
        -680,
        0
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "// Normalise the pstore kit and attach per-platform enable switches.\n// Flip a flag to true only once you have that platform's credentials.\nconst TOGGLES = { x: false, facebook: true, linkedin: true, instagram: false, pinterest: true, threads: false };\n\nconst out = [];\nfor (const it of $input.all()) {\n  const j = it.json ?? {};\n  const raw = String(j.platform ?? '').toLowerCase();\n  const key = raw.includes('twitter') || raw === 'x' ? 'x'\n    : raw.includes('facebook') ? 'facebook'\n    : raw.includes('linkedin') ? 'linkedin'\n    : raw.includes('instagram') ? 'instagram'\n    : raw.includes('pinterest') ? 'pinterest'\n    : raw.includes('threads') ? 'threads' : 'unknown';\n  out.push({ json: {\n    platform: key,\n    platformRaw: String(j.platform ?? ''),\n    body: String(j.body ?? j.title ?? ''),\n    link: String(j.link ?? ''),\n    name: String(j.name ?? j.title ?? 'pstore pick'),\n    slug: String(j.slug ?? ''),\n    keyword: String(j.keyword ?? ''),\n    board: String(j.board ?? 'Deals'),\n    image: String(j.image ?? ''),\n    image_png: String(j.image_png ?? j.image ?? ''),\n    ...TOGGLES,\n  }});\n}\nreturn out;"
      },
